#. Tag: title
#: formatpara.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting Paragraphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: formatpara.docbook:12 formatpara.docbook:46 formatpara.docbook:47
#: formatpara.docbook:48 formatpara.docbook:163 formatpara.docbook:164
#: formatpara.docbook:165 formatpara.docbook:166 formatpara.docbook:236
#: formatpara.docbook:335 formatpara.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "paragraph"
msgstr "paragraf"

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "This section will detail all the options available to format paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To format a paragraph, place the cursor in the paragraph. To format more "
"than one paragraph at a time, simply <link linkend=\"select\">select the "
"paragraphs with the mouse or keyboard</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can format one or more paragraphs one of three ways:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse pointer in the paragraph and click once with the &RMB;. A "
"small menu will appear. Select <guimenuitem>Paragraph...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dialog will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Paragraph Settings</guilabel> dialog consists of five tabbed "
"sections labeled <link linkend=\"indents-and-spaces\">Indent and Spacing</"
"link>, <link linkend=\"para-aligns\">General Layout</link>, <link linkend="
"\"para-borders\">Borders</link>, <link linkend=\"para-bullets-and-numbers"
"\">Bullets/Numbering</link>, and <link linkend=\"tab-stops\">Tabulators</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatpara.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indents and Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "indent lines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "change line spacing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "keep lines and paragraphs together"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog box the spacing between lines, and the spacing between "
"paragraphs can be specified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first section of this dialog box is labeled <guilabel>Indent</guilabel>, "
"and consists of three spin boxes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left"
msgstr "Esquèrra"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter a value in this box to indent the lines of the selected paragraphs "
"away from the left margin. The first line is unaffected by this spin box. To "
"alter the first line, specify that value in the spin box labeled "
"<guilabel>First Line</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right"
msgstr "Drecha"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter a value in this spin box to indent all lines of the selected paragraph "
"(including the first line) away from the right margin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "First Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter a number in this spin box to indent the first line of a paragraph away "
"from the left margin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entering a negative value in this spin box will create a <link linkend="
"\"defhangingindent\">hanging indention</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next section is labeled <guilabel>Line Spacing</guilabel>. It consists "
"of a combo box and a spin box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The combo box determines the method of calculating the spacing between "
"lines. It has several choices:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: formatpara.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Single, 1.5 Lines and Double"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If any of these options are selected, the paragraph will have single, 1 and "
"1/2 or double spacing respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: formatpara.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Proportional"
msgstr "Proporcional"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the spin box is enabled. When you enter a number "
"in the spin box, &kword; uses that number as a multiplier for line spacing. "
"To look at it another way, if you enter 1.00 in this box, &kword; will use "
"single spacing. If you enter 2.00 in this box, &kword; will use double "
"spacing. If you enter 3.00 in this box, &kword; will use triple spacing, "
"etc. You are not limited to whole numbers. You could enter 1.87 in this box "
"and &kword; would use 1.87 line spacing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: formatpara.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line Distance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the spin box is enabled. When you enter a number "
"in the spin box, &kword; places a measured amount of space between each "
"line. As an example, if you enter 0.75 and the units used by &kword; are "
"inches, then &kword; will place 0.75 inches between each line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: formatpara.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "At least"
msgstr "Al mens"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This sets the minimum line spacing value. This can be useful if you have "
"paragraphs with widely differing font sizes. Typically, &kword; calculates "
"the distance between lines by looking at the tallest character in the line. "
"You can use this feature to overide close linespacing in small font "
"paragraphs to make them even with large font paragraphs. &kword; will not "
"cause any fonts to overlap using this spacing technique."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: formatpara.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fixed"
msgstr "Fixe"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This sets the distance between the tops of each line to a specific unit of "
"measure. If this option is set too small, &kword; will overlap characters, "
"which will obscure the bottom parts of the characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This should not be confused with <guilabel>Line Distance</guilabel> which "
"inserts a specific unit of space between lines. <guilabel>Fixed</guilabel> "
"specifies the distance between the top of one line and the top of the next "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last section is labeled <guilabel>Paragraph Space</guilabel>. It "
"consists of two entries:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Before"
msgstr "Abans"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "By entering a value here, additional spacing is added before each paragraph."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "After"
msgstr "Aprèp"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "By entering a value here, additional spacing is added after each paragraph."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right of the dialog box, is a preview box, which will "
"<emphasis>approximate</emphasis> the final layout of your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatpara.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "justification"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "center paragraph"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "left/right aligns"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "horizontally align paragraphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section determines how the text is placed <emphasis>within the line</"
"emphasis>. With other applications, you may have referred to this simply as "
"<emphasis>alignment</emphasis>, or <emphasis>justification</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once again, a preview pane is shown on the right side of the dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the upper left corner of the dialog box is a section labeled "
"<guilabel>Alignment</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <guilabel>Left</guilabel>, <guilabel>Right</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Center</guilabel> are selected, the text will be moved on the line "
"so that it aligns with the left margin, aligns with the right margin, or is "
"centered between the margins respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <guilabel>Justify</guilabel> is selected, &kword; will increase the space "
"<emphasis>between</emphasis> words, so that each line (with the exception of "
"the last line in a paragraph), reaches both the left and right margins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use toolbar buttons to quickly change the justification of one or "
"more paragraphs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Button"
msgstr "Boton"

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command"
msgstr "Comanda"

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left Align"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Center Align"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Align"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "Justify Text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The lower section controls how &kword; divides paragraphs when a paragraph "
"will not fit entirely within the current frame or page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first option is labeled <guilabel>Keep lines together</guilabel>. If "
"this option is selected, then all of the lines of the paragraph will remain "
"on the same page. If this is not selected, &kword; may choose to move part "
"of a paragraph to a new page or frame. For most work, this option is usually "
"left unchecked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next two options are labeled <guilabel>Insert Break Before Paragraph</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Insert Break After Paragraph</guilabel>. When one of "
"these options is checked, and the paragraph moves to the next frame in the "
"frame set, a hard frame break will be inserted in front of the current "
"paragraph or after the previous paragraph (depending on the option "
"selected). This will serve to keep the paragraph in the next frame, even if "
"text prior to that frame is deleted. This option is often used in "
"conjunction with <guilabel>Keep lines together</guilabel>, to ensure that "
"the paragraph does not creep back onto the page during editing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatpara.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Decorations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "borders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next section is used to define the background color of the current "
"paragraphs and configure graphical borders around your paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the color button to the right of <guilabel>Background color:</"
"guilabel>, will let you select a color to serve as the background of your "
"paragraph."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can surround (on some or all sides) a paragraph with a border. This "
"border can be solid or not, of any color and of many sizes. This dialog "
"panel is used to adjust the borders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "Style"
msgstr "Estil"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use this combo box to select the overall type of the new border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "The choices are previewed in each selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Width"
msgstr "Largor"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will determine how wide the resulting border will be. It is measured in "
"points."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: formatpara.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color"
msgstr "Color"

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the color bar will allow you to select a color using the <link "
"linkend=\"select-colors\">color selection dialog box</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that it is determined how the borders should look, specify which edges "
"of the paragraphs need borders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select/Unselect <guiicon>Left Border</guiicon>. Clicking this button will "
"apply the current options to the left paragraph border. Clicking a second "
"time will remove the left paragraph border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select/Unselect <guiicon>Right Border</guiicon>. Clicking this button will "
"apply the current options to the right paragraph border. Clicking a second "
"time will remove the right paragraph border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select/Unselect <guiicon>Top Border</guiicon>. Clicking this button will "
"apply the current options to the top paragraph border. Clicking a second "
"time will remove the top paragraph border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: formatpara.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select/Unselect <guiicon>Bottom Border</guiicon>. Clicking this button will "
"apply the current options to the bottom paragraph border. Clicking a second "
"time will remove the bottom paragraph border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is possible to mix and match border styles, widths and colors in one "
"paragraph."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply determine the border style, width and color for one border edge, and "
"select the border using the border buttons. Now alter the style width or "
"color to create a new border look and click the new border button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Preview</guilabel> window will show you how your paragraph "
"borders will look."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatpara.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bullets and Numbering"
msgstr "Piuses e numerotacion"

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "bulleted"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: formatpara.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "numbered"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: formatpara.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A very common element of a document, is a list of items. The list contains "
"several elements which may be numbered, for easy reference. Alternatively, "
"the list elements may be simply set off from the rest of the text with a "
"special character preceding each element. These special characters are "
"called bullets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog box is used to define your bullets or the numbering method of "
"lists in the document. This dialog box can also be used to number chapters "
"and sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top section of the dialog box has three options: <guilabel>None</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>List</guilabel> and <guilabel>Chapter</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <guilabel>None</guilabel> is selected, the text is not marked as either a "
"list or a chapter. No other features of this dialog box will alter the text "
"when this option is chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>List</guilabel> is used to create lists in the document. These "
"lists are automatically numbered and formatted to appear similar. For more "
"information on lists, see the section entitled <link linkend=\"lists"
"\">Lists</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Chapter</guilabel> is used to number chapters and sections of a "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: formatpara.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tabulators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: formatpara.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog is used to adjust the tab stops. For more details, see <link "
"linkend=\"tab-stops\">Using Tab Stops</link>."
msgstr ""

